  <data name="AboutQuirks" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quirk: the tree shows the names devices give themselves. A USB 3 hub is two hubs, one on each bus, and many hub chips call their USB 2 half "USB2.1 Hub" and their USB 3 half "USB3.1 Hub" or "USB3.2 Hub". There is no USB 2.1: the "2.1" means a USB 2.0 hub with extra power saving.</value>
